1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,480
All depicted events are fictional

2
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:05,520
and for entertainment purposes only.
viewer discretion is advised.

3
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:23,320
Grant me your forgiveness,
I beg of you, Klao.

4
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:34,560
<i>So…</i>

5
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:35,800
<i>Which temple is it?</i>

6
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:39,160
<i>Wat Sema Muang.</i>

7
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:58,360
<i>My father brought me to that temple.</i>

8
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:00,120
<i>Is it true that the meeting place</i>

9
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:04,519
<i>lies in the woods behind it, Pim?</i>

10
00:01:04,599 --> 00:01:08,840
<i>Indeed, on the second watch</i>
<i>of the 15th night of the waning moon,</i>

11
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:16,680
<i>the opium trade shall occur</i>
<i>at the hut by the river every month.</i>

12
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:26,200
<i>Klao, are you certain that</i>
<i>you shall not inform the patrolmen?</i>

13
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:30,680
<i>I must witness it with my own eyes.</i>

14
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:34,640
<i>To report it to them without certainty</i>

15
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:37,400
<i>may serve only to tarnish</i>
<i>both Phop's name and my own.</i>

16
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:00,120
Are you courting death?

17
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:22,960
Where is he?

18
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:41,280
Klao!

19
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:42,360
Show yourself!

20
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:45,040
Find him, or you shall not live!

21
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:46,640
-Everyone…
-Move!

22
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:13,600
Do you think you can escape me?

23
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:35,080
You are far more stubborn
than your father.

24
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:41,560
I seek no quarrel with you.

25
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:42,920
But you!

26
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:46,960
You refuse to let us be.

27
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:49,360
Your meddling
has at last exhausted his patience.

28
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:52,480
He ordered me
to send you to hell with your father.

29
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:58,560
If this is my end,

30
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:03,440
then I shall drag you all,
you scum of the earth,

31
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:04,720
down into hell with me.

32
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:28,120
Mark me a place
in the depths of hell then!

33
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,120
Klao!

34
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:44,280
Unless…

35
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:47,600
you change your mind and join us.

36
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:51,440
The opium trade flows with gold.

37
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:54,640
One may make a fortune overnight.

38
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:59,600
If you serve as our informer,

39
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:01,600
feeding us news,

40
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:03,600
the words of your superiors,

41
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:07,720
and every move
your brother Lord Phop makes,

42
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,960
you may be handsomely rewarded.

43
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:14,760
What say you, Klao?

44
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:18,520
If you are wise, accept the offer,

45
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:21,600
and I shall spare your life.

46
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,000
Not in this life.

47
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:14,240
You are as stubborn as ever.

48
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:21,400
Pim,

49
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,720
why must you do this to me?

50
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,600
For a mere handful of coins,

51
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:44,480
you chose to stoop this low?

52
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:48,120
I seek redemption
and life far from the capital.

53
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:53,200
What more could a woman
such as I ever hope for?

54
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:57,160
Back then,

55
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,200
I truly hoped you would capture Cherd,

56
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:04,120
so that he would no longer be in my life.

57
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:07,440
When you failed,

58
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:10,800
I was truly devastated,
and that remains so.

59
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,760
But now,

60
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:20,400
you have uncovered too much.

61
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:25,400
I am the one in danger.

62
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:26,680
Cease this, Pim.

63
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,160
Kla,

64
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:31,560
leave at once before anyone finds you.

65
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:38,800
What of the promise to grant me--

66
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:40,360
Begone, I say!

67
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:46,080
He shall see to it
once you reach Pak Nam Pho.

68
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:49,960
I have readied the vessel.

69
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:52,280
Begone at once

70
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:55,280
As you wish.

71
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:01,720
Grant me your forgiveness, Master Klao.

72
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,120
Wait!

73
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:17,760
Pim!

74
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:19,920
There is no way out to the river!

75
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,560
It is but a pond. It leads nowhere!

76
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:23,280
What? What are you doing?

77
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:34,880
Such is the nature of this world, Klao.

78
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:07,360
When I returned,

79
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:11,120
I prayed that you had lost
your memory forever, as the rumors had it.

80
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:14,280
Yet you remain as stubborn as a mule,

81
00:10:15,640 --> 00:10:18,320
digging into the past
until you recalled everything.

82
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:22,520
Klao, I wish to know
how you managed to escape death.

83
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:28,040
I saw my men throw you
into the pond with my own eyes.

84
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:33,960
And I shall do the very same
to Pim and Kla.

85
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,040
Klao,

86
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:45,360
are you some kind of spirit?

87
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:47,480
What unholy power do you possess? Huh?

88
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:49,560
Answer me!

89
00:10:52,640 --> 00:10:54,520
Finish me off once again at this instant,

90
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,240
before Phop comes to save me.

91
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:17,280
Your foolishness remains unchanged.

92
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:20,880
I never took your life, Klao.

93
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:44,400
What did he say?

94
00:11:45,440 --> 00:11:46,640
He refused.

95
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,000
You have left me no choice in this, Klao.

96
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:38,000
You claim this meddling

97
00:12:40,520 --> 00:12:42,520
is for your father's sake,

98
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:48,720
but I too do this for my father.

99
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:11,080
Bid the world farewell, Klao.

100
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:34,280
Cherd.

101
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:35,920
Yes, my Lord…

102
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:40,800
Send him to his grave.

103
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:42,920
Yes, my Lord.

104
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:07,120
Lord Harn was the one who dealt the blow.

105
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:10,040
I merely cleaned up his mess.

106
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:14,360
But tonight, I shall send you
to your watery grave by my own hand.

107
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:15,760
What say you, Klao?

108
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:18,000
Agonizing, is it not?

109
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:26,560
Fear not that you will be alone in hell,

110
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:31,680
for your good brother

111
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:34,800
shall soon join you.

112
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:37,640
No, wait.

113
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:43,360
You two shall be together tonight.

114
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:44,960
Splendid, is it not?

115
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:46,720
Wonderful, is it not? Is it not?

116
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:52,720
Make haste!

117
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:53,640
At once!

118
00:15:04,880 --> 00:15:06,160
Lay down your sword.

119
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:11,560
Lay down your sword, I say!

120
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:24,600
Patrolmen.

121
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:36,840
You were so near to escaping your fate.

122
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:40,320
Had you wed Lady Varna,

123
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:43,440
we would have been family,

124
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:46,280
allowing me to keep a closer eye on you.

125
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:49,600
We would not have come to this.

126
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:01,320
What gave me away?

127
00:16:02,760 --> 00:16:04,120
Was it the absence of a pond?

128
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:06,720
I saw right through you long ago.

129
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:10,200
Every time we close in
on those opium traffickers,

130
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:13,080
they manage to slip through our fingers.

131
00:16:14,520 --> 00:16:16,840
And when the time comes for interrogation,

132
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:19,720
none are willing to confess.

133
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:21,840
The soldiers captured the smugglers

134
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:24,600
who carried opium
from the capital to sell in Sam Khok.

135
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:27,040
My father conducted
the interrogation himself,

136
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:29,480
yet none of them would confess.

137
00:16:29,560 --> 00:16:32,000
Who would dare
to implicate their own master,

138
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:33,840
and do so to his face?

139
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:40,880
But what clearly gave you away

140
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:43,480
was the poisoning of the patrolmen.

141
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:48,600
To make them lower their guard
and become intoxicated

142
00:16:50,040 --> 00:16:51,240
would require an insider.

143
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:53,360
It smells of burnt beans.

144
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:55,160
Are they castor beans?

145
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:58,280
These people were poisoned.

146
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:04,240
<i>And there is also Kla.</i>

147
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:08,079
Unless it was someone
of equal rank to mine or higher,

148
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:12,760
he could not have been
bought as an informant.

149
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:19,400
Every trail leads to you and your father.

150
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:25,119
You are far too clever for your own good.

151
00:17:26,119 --> 00:17:27,640
But if you are truly so bright,

152
00:17:28,720 --> 00:17:30,360
why did you follow me here?

153
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:33,440
Merely to buy time.

154
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:41,040
By now, your father has surely been
captured by my father's men.

155
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,680
<i>High Lord Phichaiphakdi.</i>

156
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:56,200
By what means did you find out

157
00:17:57,120 --> 00:17:58,000
that it was I?

158
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:00,640
The document.

159
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:04,760
It bears Lord Preechaphibal's name,

160
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:07,920
with a smudge running from left to right.

161
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:11,000
The handwriting is identical.

162
00:18:12,280 --> 00:18:14,360
Yet my father never smudged ink.

163
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:17,600
Why then is there
a smudge here and nowhere else?

164
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:21,120
Hence, the forger…

165
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:24,960
must be…

166
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:26,320
left-handed.

167
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:33,080
High Lord.

168
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:35,680
We are officials of the state,

169
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:39,280
entrusted with the duty
of safeguarding the welfare of the people.

170
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:43,040
Having been granted a life
far more bountiful than the common folk,

171
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:46,520
we cannot commit such an act.

172
00:18:51,120 --> 00:18:52,800
Pray, accept it.

173
00:18:54,040 --> 00:18:56,200
I merely need you to act

174
00:18:56,280 --> 00:18:58,600
as my intermediary
with the Farangi and the Chinese.

175
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:02,400
Nothing will be traced back to you.
You have my assurance.

176
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:10,560
I shall accept only your kindness.

177
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:13,840
As for all else,

178
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:18,240
I must most respectfully decline.

179
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:23,200
Should any word of opium smuggling
reach me from the capital,

180
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:25,040
I fear…

181
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:27,880
you shall be the first…

182
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:30,840
I suspect.

183
00:19:38,240 --> 00:19:39,120
Be that as it may,

184
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:44,840
remain here
and wallow in your misery in Phichit.

185
00:19:46,840 --> 00:19:48,080
<i>Lord Preechaphibal</i>

186
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:50,920
was a man of many talents,

187
00:19:51,600 --> 00:19:53,360
yet he was a fool.

188
00:19:55,920 --> 00:20:00,480
The moment I summoned him
to the capital in your name,

189
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:02,760
he recklessly came,

190
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:06,120
believing he could lend you his aid.

191
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:08,800
That trickery

192
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:11,840
presented me the perfect opportunity

193
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:14,400
to steal his personal seal

194
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:17,280
and forge the document.

195
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:26,360
High Lord.

196
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:28,200
High Lord…

197
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:48,040
How pitiful.

198
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:53,880
It is a shame

199
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:59,600
that you are just as foolish
as your dearest friend.

200
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:02,000
You shall never know,

201
00:21:02,080 --> 00:21:03,240
not in the slightest,

202
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:08,440
that Meng and I conspired
to poison your tea.

203
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:14,640
With this settled,

204
00:21:15,680 --> 00:21:17,800
Lord Preechaphibal's secret

205
00:21:19,520 --> 00:21:22,000
shall go to the grave with you.

206
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:28,120
Your Excellency, an opium shipment list
has been found beneath his manor.

207
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:42,280
So, you lured me out
to lead me into a trap, High Lord?

208
00:21:42,360 --> 00:21:43,320
Precisely.

209
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:46,000
Now then,

210
00:21:46,080 --> 00:21:50,920
who is the fool at this hour, High Lord?

211
00:21:58,840 --> 00:22:00,320
So Meng…

212
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:04,720
has chosen to turn against me?

213
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:06,480
Meng…

214
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:10,800
simply chose to stand
on the side of justice.

215
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:13,960
Phop visits this teahouse frequently.

216
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:17,800
Meng would never dare poison me.

217
00:22:22,120 --> 00:22:23,120
It is not over.

218
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:26,240
Though you may have eluded my poison,

219
00:22:27,080 --> 00:22:30,040
my men are already upon you.

220
00:22:30,120 --> 00:22:31,200
Soldiers!

221
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:35,480
Lay waste to
High Lord Phichaiphakdi at once!

222
00:22:38,360 --> 00:22:39,200
Soldiers!

223
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:41,560
Soldiers!

224
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:05,240
Accept your fate, High Lord.

225
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:09,480
To resist or flee
would only bring you further disgrace.

226
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:11,360
This way.

227
00:23:30,520 --> 00:23:31,760
Any news of Lord Phop?

228
00:23:32,840 --> 00:23:34,320
He has yet to arrive.

229
00:23:34,840 --> 00:23:38,120
However, we have already
sent reinforcements to assist him.

230
00:24:12,120 --> 00:24:13,800
Surrender now, Phop!

231
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:15,080
You shall not escape!

232
00:24:33,760 --> 00:24:35,400
You have been defeated, Lord Harn.

233
00:24:36,160 --> 00:24:38,000
The cell awaits.

234
00:24:38,080 --> 00:24:40,280
Then you shall fall with me!

235
00:24:40,360 --> 00:24:42,040
By now, Klao…

236
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:44,640
has certainly been slaughtered by Cherd.

237
00:24:46,560 --> 00:24:49,400
You asked after Klao this evening,
did you not?

238
00:24:49,480 --> 00:24:51,200
Then hear me well!

239
00:24:53,240 --> 00:24:55,320
Cherd conspired with Pim,

240
00:24:55,960 --> 00:24:57,760
hiding in the Pavilion of Affection

241
00:24:59,120 --> 00:25:00,640
to ensnare Klao.

242
00:25:01,480 --> 00:25:04,120
He must surely be in Cherd's hands by now.

243
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:09,920
At last,

244
00:25:10,880 --> 00:25:13,000
Klao had once again been slain,

245
00:25:15,080 --> 00:25:18,040
despite my having already killed him.

246
00:25:30,920 --> 00:25:32,120
Seize that Harn at once!

247
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:33,200
I shall save Klao!

248
00:25:33,280 --> 00:25:34,160
Yes, my Lord!

249
00:25:54,920 --> 00:25:58,480
<i>Wat Bot, oh, the temple of old</i>

250
00:26:00,720 --> 00:26:03,600
<i>Where seven toddy palms stand tall as told</i>

251
00:26:07,200 --> 00:26:10,000
<i>Khun Thong went forth on the raid</i>

252
00:26:12,880 --> 00:26:15,840
<i>He has yet to return</i>
<i>For the sweet embrace</i>

253
00:26:19,560 --> 00:26:22,240
<i>Wrapping food in a bundle</i>

254
00:26:23,680 --> 00:26:26,400
<i>I rowed out to look for my angel</i>

255
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:30,560
<i>Yet the rumors had already spread</i>

256
00:26:32,200 --> 00:26:33,680
<i>That Khun Thong had met</i>

257
00:26:34,880 --> 00:26:36,000
<i>His fate</i>

258
00:27:02,720 --> 00:27:03,720
It is time.

259
00:27:04,400 --> 00:27:06,680
Let us send Klao to a watery grave.

260
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:09,920
Still here, are you not, Cherd?

261
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:11,840
My Lord. Oh, my Lord.

262
00:27:11,920 --> 00:27:13,000
I shall depart at once.

263
00:27:13,080 --> 00:27:15,280
This time, he shall meet his end.

264
00:27:27,120 --> 00:27:28,080
Hey! Unhand me!

265
00:27:28,160 --> 00:27:29,160
Unhand me at once!

266
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:30,080
You scoundrel!

267
00:27:30,160 --> 00:27:31,160
Cherd.

268
00:27:31,640 --> 00:27:33,120
Cherd, Cherd!

269
00:27:33,200 --> 00:27:34,040
Cherd!

270
00:27:39,080 --> 00:27:39,920
Klao…

271
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:42,920
Klao…

272
00:27:44,480 --> 00:27:45,720
Klao.

273
00:27:46,280 --> 00:27:47,240
Klao.

274
00:27:51,880 --> 00:27:52,800
Klao.

275
00:27:53,800 --> 00:27:54,640
Klao.

276
00:27:56,320 --> 00:27:57,880
My deepest thanks to you,

277
00:27:58,400 --> 00:27:59,360
Kaew

278
00:28:00,320 --> 00:28:01,320
and Jom.

279
00:28:03,040 --> 00:28:04,920
You are in good hands now, Klao.

280
00:28:33,440 --> 00:28:34,320
And…

281
00:28:35,200 --> 00:28:36,360
Cherd's men…

282
00:28:36,880 --> 00:28:37,720
They…

283
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:42,400
cast Pim and Kla into the pond.

284
00:28:53,640 --> 00:28:54,600
Jom!

285
00:28:54,680 --> 00:28:55,600
Blood…

286
00:29:06,400 --> 00:29:07,680
It is Cherd's.

287
00:29:13,280 --> 00:29:14,720
You have my heartfelt thanks,

288
00:29:16,320 --> 00:29:17,760
my dearest Kaew.

289
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:39,960
Rise.

290
00:29:40,440 --> 00:29:41,480
I am guiltless!

291
00:29:43,160 --> 00:29:44,080
I am innocent!

292
00:29:44,800 --> 00:29:45,640
Have you gone mad?

293
00:29:45,720 --> 00:29:47,840
I am merely protecting my master!

294
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:49,360
It was he who meddled with us!

295
00:29:50,600 --> 00:29:51,960
You!

296
00:29:52,040 --> 00:29:54,480
Damn you, Klao! You are the cause of this!

297
00:29:54,560 --> 00:29:56,800
I shall drag you into the depths of hell!

298
00:29:58,920 --> 00:30:00,480
Cease this blaming at once, Cherd!

299
00:30:02,480 --> 00:30:04,440
You are a wretched opium smoker
and a peddler.

300
00:30:05,720 --> 00:30:07,840
You attempted to murder Klao
to bury the truth.

301
00:30:09,280 --> 00:30:11,960
You took Pim's life
solely to save your own.

302
00:30:13,880 --> 00:30:15,480
Your stupidity matches your malice.

303
00:30:16,560 --> 00:30:18,720
No one is to blame for your actions.

304
00:30:30,080 --> 00:30:31,360
I ended Pim's life…

305
00:30:36,840 --> 00:30:38,160
I killed her.

306
00:30:38,240 --> 00:30:39,680
Pim, forgive me.

307
00:30:43,240 --> 00:30:44,160
I killed her.

308
00:30:44,240 --> 00:30:45,280
I killed her…

309
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:49,800
I murdered her!

310
00:30:55,880 --> 00:30:58,480
I am sorry, Pim. Forgive me.

311
00:30:58,560 --> 00:30:59,400
Take him away.

312
00:31:00,600 --> 00:31:01,440
Yes, my Lord.

313
00:31:08,080 --> 00:31:09,440
Pim, I am sorry.

314
00:31:18,600 --> 00:31:19,800
Are you injured at all?

315
00:32:27,280 --> 00:32:28,760
Toast!

316
00:32:38,160 --> 00:32:40,280
My deepest thanks.

317
00:32:41,880 --> 00:32:43,120
Without you,

318
00:32:44,480 --> 00:32:46,120
I would not have survived.

319
00:32:52,600 --> 00:32:53,560
By the way…

320
00:32:54,440 --> 00:32:56,040
Jom and Kaew,

321
00:32:56,120 --> 00:32:57,960
how did you find me there?

322
00:32:59,280 --> 00:33:00,520
We owe our sincere thanks…

323
00:33:07,320 --> 00:33:08,400
to that young man.

324
00:33:12,480 --> 00:33:13,920
That long pause was a crime.

325
00:33:15,880 --> 00:33:18,160
I told Physician Jom

326
00:33:18,240 --> 00:33:20,520
that I saw a patrolman named Kla

327
00:33:20,600 --> 00:33:23,520
linger outside the tavern every night,

328
00:33:23,600 --> 00:33:26,760
speaking with Cherd in secret
once it was closed.

329
00:33:26,840 --> 00:33:28,120
They were acquainted,

330
00:33:28,200 --> 00:33:30,720
so he helped Cherd
conceal the truth about his wound.

331
00:33:30,800 --> 00:33:33,280
Furthermore,
I crossed paths with him this evening

332
00:33:33,360 --> 00:33:35,080
going to the Pavilion of Affection.

333
00:33:35,760 --> 00:33:38,240
Cherd bears Master Klao great hatred.

334
00:33:38,320 --> 00:33:39,760
This means that

335
00:33:40,320 --> 00:33:42,160
Kla was acquainted with Cherd,

336
00:33:42,960 --> 00:33:44,680
and I feared that…

337
00:33:45,400 --> 00:33:49,320
the two might conspire to ambush you

338
00:33:49,400 --> 00:33:51,040
at the Pavilion of Affection.

339
00:33:53,280 --> 00:33:55,000
Your subordinate

340
00:33:55,640 --> 00:33:57,240
is quite eloquent, is he not?

341
00:33:57,800 --> 00:33:59,280
On this night,

342
00:33:59,840 --> 00:34:03,520
he has spoken more in a single day
than in all his life.

343
00:34:07,240 --> 00:34:09,400
What happened next, Jom?

344
00:34:11,440 --> 00:34:12,760
<i>I saw Cherd here</i>

345
00:34:12,840 --> 00:34:14,600
with a certain patrolman.

346
00:34:14,679 --> 00:34:17,360
I seem to recall him being a man
under Lord Phop's command.

347
00:34:21,679 --> 00:34:23,920
This means there is a traitor
among Phop's men.

348
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:27,560
Kaew, summon the patrols here at once.

349
00:34:28,320 --> 00:34:31,040
Should anything occur,
they shall aid all of us.

350
00:34:34,600 --> 00:34:36,199
I cannot do this.

351
00:34:40,040 --> 00:34:41,400
I place my full trust in you.

352
00:34:42,360 --> 00:34:45,560
Never have I known a soul
so wise and resilient as you.

353
00:35:02,920 --> 00:35:04,680
You are capable of this, Kaew.

354
00:35:06,680 --> 00:35:09,600
We shall not let anything happen to Klao.

355
00:35:30,080 --> 00:35:32,840
Kaew, the patrolmen,
and I kept close watch.

356
00:35:32,920 --> 00:35:34,840
But Kla left the establishment with a bag.

357
00:35:34,920 --> 00:35:36,560
He left alongside Pim.

358
00:35:36,640 --> 00:35:38,640
We tracked them down to the hut.

359
00:35:40,920 --> 00:35:44,120
Unfortunately,
the route was unknown to us,

360
00:35:45,080 --> 00:35:47,640
and thus we could not save
Pim and Kla in time.

361
00:35:48,640 --> 00:35:51,360
I am already more than grateful
for your assistance.

362
00:35:51,920 --> 00:35:54,080
Cherd has now been imprisoned.

363
00:35:54,920 --> 00:35:57,800
Lord Harn is being hunted by my men.

364
00:35:58,480 --> 00:35:59,840
He will not get far.

365
00:36:02,840 --> 00:36:04,840
The truth has come to light,

366
00:36:08,800 --> 00:36:10,160
yet one thing remains unclear.

367
00:36:11,480 --> 00:36:16,200
By what means did you triumph
over the High Lord's men?

368
00:36:22,960 --> 00:36:23,920
Master.

369
00:36:26,680 --> 00:36:28,920
A-Chai, step back.
Retreat for but a moment.

370
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:31,040
Calm yourselves, fellow soldiers.

371
00:36:31,120 --> 00:36:32,960
No need for such haste.

372
00:36:33,040 --> 00:36:35,760
Would you like some tea?
We have a kettle full here.

373
00:36:36,440 --> 00:36:38,520
After taking a sip,

374
00:36:38,600 --> 00:36:41,520
you are free to cut off my head,
should that be your wish.

375
00:36:41,600 --> 00:36:44,160
Behold, in this kettle is Da Hong Pao.

376
00:36:44,240 --> 00:36:45,440
It rejuvenates your soul.

377
00:36:45,520 --> 00:36:48,000
It is the very tea favored by
the current Emperor himself.

378
00:36:48,080 --> 00:36:50,680
It calms your soul

379
00:36:50,760 --> 00:36:55,280
as if a bodhisattva's chant
were echoing within your heart.

380
00:37:03,960 --> 00:37:05,120
Hey!

381
00:37:09,080 --> 00:37:10,760
-One. Two.
-Two.

382
00:37:10,840 --> 00:37:11,880
-Three.
-Three.

383
00:37:11,960 --> 00:37:12,960
-Enjoy!
-Enjoy!

384
00:37:21,200 --> 00:37:22,560
Form a circle.

385
00:37:22,640 --> 00:37:25,840
Have them circle around
until they lose their senses.

386
00:37:25,920 --> 00:37:27,320
Circle around.

387
00:37:27,400 --> 00:37:28,760
Around and around.

388
00:37:38,880 --> 00:37:40,200
Curse you.

389
00:37:45,360 --> 00:37:46,720
His Excellency

390
00:37:46,800 --> 00:37:49,960
still draws breath tonight
because of my hand.

391
00:37:50,520 --> 00:37:54,360
Before calling the tavern my new home,

392
00:37:54,440 --> 00:37:56,760
I served as a patrolman myself.

393
00:37:58,240 --> 00:37:59,080
Not true.

394
00:38:00,760 --> 00:38:03,400
I shall lie when pigs fly.

395
00:38:03,480 --> 00:38:06,040
Go and smell its arse,
should you not believe me.

396
00:38:06,600 --> 00:38:08,280
Cease this folly, will you?

397
00:38:09,280 --> 00:38:11,640
During my days in China,

398
00:38:11,720 --> 00:38:14,600
I trained in martial arts
under a senior kinsman.

399
00:38:14,680 --> 00:38:16,240
He was my uncle's older brother,

400
00:38:16,320 --> 00:38:18,360
and my uncle
was my father's younger brother.

401
00:38:18,440 --> 00:38:20,360
And this man was my father's father.

402
00:38:20,440 --> 00:38:22,480
-I do not believe it.
-I trained…

403
00:38:22,560 --> 00:38:25,200
-What I have said is true.
-I could never believe you.

404
00:38:25,280 --> 00:38:27,040
A true story, I say.

405
00:38:27,120 --> 00:38:28,240
A lie, I say.

406
00:38:28,320 --> 00:38:29,200
If it was…

407
00:38:29,280 --> 00:38:31,440
-Now, now, Master.
-What of it?

408
00:38:32,000 --> 00:38:33,840
You pushed me, did you not?

409
00:38:33,920 --> 00:38:35,920
-You pushed me?
-And what of it?

410
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:37,520
You seek a challenge, do you not?

411
00:38:37,600 --> 00:38:39,080
And what of it, I ask?

412
00:38:39,160 --> 00:38:40,080
-Huh?
-Do you--

413
00:38:40,160 --> 00:38:42,760
-What of it?
-You have struck me.

414
00:38:42,840 --> 00:38:44,000
Begone.

415
00:38:44,080 --> 00:38:46,200
-Begone, I said.
-Did you lay your hand upon me?

416
00:38:46,280 --> 00:38:47,800
Did I?

417
00:38:57,920 --> 00:39:00,160
They spun a grand tale, did they not?

418
00:39:00,240 --> 00:39:02,040
In truth, they were cowering in fear,

419
00:39:02,120 --> 00:39:04,760
leaving the men of High Lord Pichayabhakdi

420
00:39:04,840 --> 00:39:07,800
to deal with those
of High Lord Horathibodi.

421
00:39:10,640 --> 00:39:11,840
Unhand me.

422
00:39:11,920 --> 00:39:14,360
-Let go. I must…
-Come.

423
00:39:14,440 --> 00:39:15,520
Come here.

424
00:39:15,600 --> 00:39:16,800
-This way.
-Come this way.

425
00:39:16,880 --> 00:39:19,200
-A man like me does not…
-I am not afraid of you.

426
00:39:19,280 --> 00:39:21,960
Let that be known. Come this way.

427
00:39:25,080 --> 00:39:26,840
Do you truly believe their words, Klao?

428
00:39:31,400 --> 00:39:33,120
Not even in the slightest.

429
00:39:35,680 --> 00:39:37,080
But if you ask

430
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:40,160
what I have gained from this mess,

431
00:39:41,160 --> 00:39:42,520
it would be that…

432
00:39:44,240 --> 00:39:46,400
I shall never again
put faith in tales of others,

433
00:39:47,600 --> 00:39:48,560
perhaps.

434
00:39:51,200 --> 00:39:52,760
This includes the words spun

435
00:39:53,480 --> 00:39:56,360
by others concerning my past.

436
00:39:58,040 --> 00:39:59,640
The stories of Pim,

437
00:40:00,320 --> 00:40:01,160
of Cherd,

438
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:02,960
of Lord Harn,

439
00:40:05,560 --> 00:40:07,040
and even those in history.

440
00:40:09,680 --> 00:40:11,080
Whoever tells their stories

441
00:40:12,160 --> 00:40:14,360
shall ever seek
to cast themselves in a good light.

442
00:40:21,040 --> 00:40:23,160
All has come to an end.

443
00:40:23,240 --> 00:40:25,320
If Lord Harn is brought to justice,

444
00:40:27,200 --> 00:40:29,400
then your mission
is undoubtedly fulfilled.

445
00:40:33,240 --> 00:40:35,120
<i>If my mission is fulfilled,</i>

446
00:40:39,160 --> 00:40:40,920
<i>it means I must return to the present.</i>

447
00:41:10,560 --> 00:41:12,360
A new day is upon us.

448
00:41:12,440 --> 00:41:14,520
The hill myna has begun to whistle.

449
00:41:15,800 --> 00:41:17,240
That is not true.

450
00:41:17,880 --> 00:41:19,840
There is an owl within.

451
00:41:22,640 --> 00:41:24,280
It is still dark outside.

452
00:41:34,720 --> 00:41:36,360
Better, is it not?

453
00:41:37,800 --> 00:41:39,680
You seemed very unwell last night.

454
00:41:40,800 --> 00:41:42,040
Well…

455
00:41:42,120 --> 00:41:44,040
I was thinking about Cherd.

456
00:41:50,040 --> 00:41:51,480
Last night,

457
00:41:52,920 --> 00:41:55,720
when his men bound me,

458
00:41:57,520 --> 00:42:00,240
Cherd sang me a lullaby.

459
00:42:00,320 --> 00:42:01,680
It made me shiver.

460
00:42:02,680 --> 00:42:05,240
The lullaby had some meaning.

461
00:42:06,200 --> 00:42:07,360
Wat Bot.

462
00:42:08,120 --> 00:42:09,680
Toddy palms.

463
00:42:10,960 --> 00:42:12,480
Khun Thong.

464
00:42:13,200 --> 00:42:14,680
<i>That Khun Thong had met</i>

465
00:42:15,920 --> 00:42:17,680
<i>His fate</i>

466
00:42:21,160 --> 00:42:23,000
He must be yearning for his father.

467
00:42:24,640 --> 00:42:26,160
My men once told me

468
00:42:27,240 --> 00:42:29,720
that his father owned a toddy palm grove.

469
00:42:30,800 --> 00:42:33,800
It was said that he fell from a height,
leaving him broken.

470
00:42:47,520 --> 00:42:49,160
Cherd loved his father dearly.

471
00:42:49,880 --> 00:42:51,280
After his father was crippled,

472
00:42:53,240 --> 00:42:55,280
Cherd's mother became a drunkard

473
00:42:58,120 --> 00:43:00,960
and began beating his father
out of exhaustion.

474
00:43:03,120 --> 00:43:04,960
In the end, he perished,

475
00:43:07,240 --> 00:43:09,760
and she descended into madness.

476
00:43:11,120 --> 00:43:13,400
That is why Cherd took refuge in opium.

477
00:43:18,400 --> 00:43:20,200
He must have been in deep sorrow.

478
00:43:20,280 --> 00:43:23,240
He often had nightmares
of his mother murdering his father.

479
00:43:28,040 --> 00:43:29,600
He likely wishes…

480
00:43:29,680 --> 00:43:31,000
to sleep without dreams.

481
00:43:34,560 --> 00:43:37,360
That is why you would not wish
for me to quarrel with him?

482
00:43:42,200 --> 00:43:43,640
And that is why

483
00:43:44,400 --> 00:43:47,120
Lord Harn gave Cherd opium,
thereby turning him into an addict.

484
00:43:47,880 --> 00:43:49,600
Cherd then became a tool.

485
00:43:51,240 --> 00:43:52,440
And Cherd…

486
00:43:52,520 --> 00:43:54,840
loves Lord Harn as his new father.

487
00:43:56,760 --> 00:43:58,520
The reason he was charmed by Pim

488
00:43:59,160 --> 00:44:02,840
was the lack of love given by a woman

489
00:44:03,400 --> 00:44:04,600
such as his own mother.

490
00:44:05,880 --> 00:44:06,960
Even Cherd

491
00:44:08,120 --> 00:44:10,640
is not a demon from hell as we thought,

492
00:44:12,000 --> 00:44:13,880
but someone has made him so.

493
00:44:18,360 --> 00:44:19,960
My dearest.

494
00:44:21,600 --> 00:44:24,160
You truly have a sympathetic heart,

495
00:44:26,400 --> 00:44:28,400
despite his having hurt you so much.

496
00:44:32,960 --> 00:44:34,240
I understood him,

497
00:44:34,320 --> 00:44:35,760
but I do not stand by his side.

498
00:44:36,640 --> 00:44:39,240
And karma has caught up with him.

499
00:44:47,280 --> 00:44:48,280
At last,

500
00:44:49,360 --> 00:44:51,480
Klao had once again been slain,

501
00:44:53,560 --> 00:44:56,520
despite my having already killed him
with my own hands.

502
00:45:11,360 --> 00:45:13,120
What ails you, Phop?

503
00:45:16,720 --> 00:45:18,320
I would ask you something.

504
00:45:20,280 --> 00:45:22,480
<i>Did he learn something from Lord Harn?</i>

505
00:45:23,320 --> 00:45:25,160
<i>Should I tell him now</i>

506
00:45:25,240 --> 00:45:26,480
<i>that I am from the future?</i>

507
00:45:27,400 --> 00:45:30,760
<i>No one knows when I'll go back either.</i>

508
00:45:38,920 --> 00:45:40,600
There is a merit-making ceremony.

509
00:45:41,560 --> 00:45:42,880
Would you like to join me?

510
00:45:52,320 --> 00:45:54,080
That said, let us go and wash ourselves.

511
00:46:15,000 --> 00:46:15,960
<i>It's fine.</i>

512
00:46:17,040 --> 00:46:18,240
<i>Focus on the present.</i>

513
00:46:18,920 --> 00:46:21,080
<i>Cherd has been arrested.</i>

514
00:46:21,160 --> 00:46:23,080
<i>Best to enjoy my time with Phop,</i>

515
00:46:24,040 --> 00:46:25,560
<i>one moment at a time.</i>

516
00:46:57,800 --> 00:46:59,480
Cherd's whereabouts remain unknown.

517
00:47:00,120 --> 00:47:02,560
The firearm taken from the Farangi
has also disappeared.

518
00:47:03,240 --> 00:47:04,760
Inform Lord Phop at once!

519
00:47:04,840 --> 00:47:06,840
He and Master Klao are in grave danger!

520
00:49:06,520 --> 00:49:08,160
Your prayers were extensive, Phop.

521
00:49:11,240 --> 00:49:12,920
Will the Buddha take heed of that?

522
00:49:16,120 --> 00:49:18,640
I call upon the Buddha as my witness.

523
00:49:19,680 --> 00:49:22,280
My heart belongs to you alone,
and ever shall it remain.

524
00:49:25,400 --> 00:49:27,560
I shall approach my parents

525
00:49:29,360 --> 00:49:30,840
to ask for your hand in marriage.

526
00:49:36,320 --> 00:49:39,440
Then I shall cherish
and protect the very heart of my life

527
00:49:40,560 --> 00:49:41,920
until the end of my days.

528
00:49:46,200 --> 00:49:47,760
This is another wish of mine.

529
00:49:50,280 --> 00:49:52,600
Should there be another lifetime,

530
00:49:53,160 --> 00:49:55,120
we shall seek each other out once more.

531
00:49:58,280 --> 00:50:00,040
May our love remain steadfast,

532
00:50:01,400 --> 00:50:03,240
though the tides of time may turn.

533
00:50:08,600 --> 00:50:09,440
But…

534
00:50:11,080 --> 00:50:12,600
after this day,

535
00:50:13,400 --> 00:50:14,840
if I am gone,

536
00:50:18,440 --> 00:50:20,200
promise me you will live well.

537
00:50:21,800 --> 00:50:22,680
No.

538
00:50:36,440 --> 00:50:38,280
I shall seek you out…

539
00:50:39,200 --> 00:50:40,520
until I find you

540
00:50:42,600 --> 00:50:44,320
and love you once more.

541
00:51:23,240 --> 00:51:24,760
Do you remember that shop?

542
00:51:26,120 --> 00:51:28,320
We should choose new rings.

543
00:51:33,400 --> 00:51:34,800
This one is my favorite.

544
00:51:37,040 --> 00:51:38,160
Good heavens!

545
00:51:38,240 --> 00:51:40,720
I must have taken it off when I bathed.

546
00:51:41,240 --> 00:51:42,920
I forgot to put it back on.

547
00:51:44,360 --> 00:51:45,720
Think no more of it.

548
00:51:46,280 --> 00:51:48,480
We shall procure a finer ring than that.

549
00:51:49,200 --> 00:51:50,640
Which kind do you prefer?

550
00:51:50,720 --> 00:51:52,520
I shall engrave it upon my heart

551
00:51:54,160 --> 00:51:57,000
for when the time comes
to acquire your wedding ring.

552
00:52:22,720 --> 00:52:24,440
-Cherd!
-How did he get here?

553
00:52:24,520 --> 00:52:25,360
Run! Now!

554
00:52:30,120 --> 00:52:31,120
Make way!

555
00:52:46,240 --> 00:52:47,840
We can go no further.

556
00:52:48,800 --> 00:52:50,280
You must hide here.

557
00:52:51,120 --> 00:52:52,560
I shall go and seize him.

558
00:52:53,320 --> 00:52:54,680
No, I beg you!

559
00:52:55,680 --> 00:52:57,120
What if we part again?

560
00:52:57,760 --> 00:52:59,360
Many times have we been parted,

561
00:52:59,920 --> 00:53:01,800
yet ever do I find my way to you.

562
00:53:06,920 --> 00:53:08,080
I promise you,

563
00:53:09,920 --> 00:53:11,080
I shall return.

564
00:53:12,440 --> 00:53:14,520
Nothing shall ever part us again.

565
00:53:22,600 --> 00:53:24,480
Klao!

566
00:53:28,760 --> 00:53:30,560
You shall never escape my grasp!

567
00:53:32,400 --> 00:53:34,160
Your sins are too great to bear, Cherd!

568
00:53:35,480 --> 00:53:36,720
I beg of you, let me go.

569
00:53:37,840 --> 00:53:38,800
Hear me well,

570
00:53:38,880 --> 00:53:40,520
or you shall be sentenced to death.

571
00:53:40,600 --> 00:53:41,880
I care not!

572
00:53:43,880 --> 00:53:47,080
You must die by my hand alone!

573
00:53:47,160 --> 00:53:48,280
Lower the firearm!

574
00:53:49,120 --> 00:53:49,960
Cease this!

575
00:53:50,520 --> 00:53:53,600
Or else, you shall be sent
to the depths of hell!

576
00:53:55,640 --> 00:53:57,280
Should I be sent there,

577
00:53:59,680 --> 00:54:01,760
then I shall drag you down with me!

578
00:54:51,960 --> 00:54:53,760
<i>I shall seek you out…</i>

579
00:54:54,760 --> 00:54:56,400
<i>until I find you</i>

580
00:54:58,240 --> 00:54:59,920
<i>and love you once more.</i>

581
00:55:01,360 --> 00:55:02,280
Phop!

582
00:55:11,640 --> 00:55:13,040
Phop, where are you?

583
00:55:15,800 --> 00:55:16,720
Phop.

584
00:55:38,600 --> 00:55:39,760
I'm back home?

585
00:56:23,040 --> 00:56:24,120
Nakun!

586
00:56:25,360 --> 00:56:26,280
Nakun, my dear!

587
00:56:27,800 --> 00:56:28,640
Nakun!

588
00:56:29,240 --> 00:56:30,280
That way.

589
00:56:30,360 --> 00:56:31,200
That way!

590
00:56:31,680 --> 00:56:32,520
<i>Mom…</i>

591
00:56:33,680 --> 00:56:34,520
<i>Is that you?</i>

592
00:56:41,920 --> 00:56:42,760
He has come to.

593
00:56:42,840 --> 00:56:44,480
Hey, can you hear me?

594
00:56:44,560 --> 00:56:46,400
If you do, please blink.

595
00:56:46,480 --> 00:56:48,520
Are you injured in any way?

596
00:56:50,800 --> 00:56:51,680
Nakun.

597
00:56:53,000 --> 00:56:54,200
Sweetie!

598
00:56:55,680 --> 00:56:56,640
My dear.

599
00:56:57,240 --> 00:56:58,080
Nakun.

600
00:57:06,080 --> 00:57:06,960
Mom.

601
00:57:08,440 --> 00:57:10,080
Is this really you?

602
00:57:12,640 --> 00:57:14,720
Of course, it's me.

603
00:57:15,520 --> 00:57:16,360
Nakun…

604
00:57:17,760 --> 00:57:18,600
What's the matter?

605
00:57:18,680 --> 00:57:20,840
What's wrong? Are you hurt?

606
00:57:20,920 --> 00:57:22,040
Tell me where it hurts.

607
00:57:25,080 --> 00:57:27,840
Please take me to Phop, Mom.

608
00:57:36,360 --> 00:57:38,960
Mom, please take me to Phop.

609
00:57:39,040 --> 00:57:40,320
My dear…

610
00:57:59,720 --> 00:58:02,360
Seeing you healthy is all I could ask for.

611
00:58:02,440 --> 00:58:05,000
The doctor told you to rest a lot.

612
00:58:05,720 --> 00:58:08,600
Get some rest, okay?

613
00:58:14,320 --> 00:58:15,320
Dear.

614
00:58:18,800 --> 00:58:20,400
Is something wrong?

615
00:58:21,280 --> 00:58:23,120
Tell me if anything is bothering you.

616
00:58:26,080 --> 00:58:27,000
Dear…

617
00:58:29,520 --> 00:58:32,080
what were you doing
at the orchard all night?

618
00:58:41,960 --> 00:58:43,520
All night?

619
00:58:45,080 --> 00:58:46,280
Yes, you heard me.

620
00:58:46,360 --> 00:58:48,240
You even had a bottle of alcohol.

621
00:58:49,040 --> 00:58:49,960
Nakun…

622
00:58:52,400 --> 00:58:54,880
You can tell me
what's stressing you out, okay?

623
00:58:59,360 --> 00:59:00,360
How…

624
00:59:01,200 --> 00:59:03,800
long was I out?

625
00:59:06,120 --> 00:59:08,080
I don't really know either.

626
00:59:08,160 --> 00:59:12,000
It was past 11 p.m.
when I got back from the wedding.

627
00:59:12,080 --> 00:59:14,240
You were already gone when I got home.

628
00:59:14,320 --> 00:59:17,920
And I thought
you went to get something around here.

629
00:59:18,880 --> 00:59:23,040
I waited for so long,
but you still hadn't come back.

630
00:59:23,760 --> 00:59:26,480
You didn't bring
your phone with you either.

631
00:59:27,480 --> 00:59:28,480
I thought

632
00:59:29,160 --> 00:59:31,920
things were starting to feel a bit off.

633
00:59:32,680 --> 00:59:35,080
Then I saw you lying there in the orchard…

634
00:59:35,720 --> 00:59:37,960
And you were wearing
some very odd clothes.

635
00:59:40,880 --> 00:59:43,240
I tried so hard to wake you up…

636
00:59:44,320 --> 00:59:45,840
but you wouldn't open your eyes.

637
00:59:46,800 --> 00:59:48,120
I was so horrified…

638
00:59:48,800 --> 00:59:51,160
that I called emergency services.

639
00:59:51,240 --> 00:59:52,200
And…

640
00:59:52,680 --> 00:59:54,600
in less than an hour,

641
00:59:55,240 --> 00:59:56,840
you woke up.

642
01:00:01,360 --> 01:00:02,800
Less than an hour?

643
01:00:03,720 --> 01:00:04,560
Nakun.

644
01:00:06,520 --> 01:00:08,320
It had been less than an hour,

645
01:00:08,400 --> 01:00:11,200
but my heart almost couldn't take it.

646
01:00:13,760 --> 01:00:16,640
I was terrified something bad
had happened to you.

647
01:00:50,120 --> 01:00:51,520
<i>The professor said that</i>

648
01:00:52,480 --> 01:00:53,920
<i>upon completing the mission,</i>

649
01:00:54,960 --> 01:00:56,800
<i>the character could return to their world.</i>

650
01:00:57,440 --> 01:00:58,400
However,

651
01:00:59,240 --> 01:01:03,280
should the main character
fail their mission,

652
01:01:04,760 --> 01:01:07,400
the portal would be closed forever,

653
01:01:07,480 --> 01:01:11,400
preventing their return to their world.

654
01:01:12,480 --> 01:01:13,360
<i>That's a lie.</i>

655
01:01:14,320 --> 01:01:16,640
<i>Even though we knew who the culprit was,</i>

656
01:01:17,800 --> 01:01:19,480
<i>Cherd managed to escape.</i>

657
01:01:20,800 --> 01:01:22,600
<i>Harn is also still at large.</i>

658
01:01:23,840 --> 01:01:25,800
<i>How can my mission be complete?</i>

659
01:01:26,680 --> 01:01:30,400
If you can't manage a full meal,
at least have some fruit.

660
01:01:59,640 --> 01:02:01,560
<i>It is of the finest quality,</i>

661
01:02:02,120 --> 01:02:03,800
brought by traders from China.

662
01:02:06,600 --> 01:02:08,000
Thanks.

663
01:02:08,720 --> 01:02:09,560
<i>Phop.</i>

664
01:02:10,800 --> 01:02:12,440
<i>I wonder how you're doing.</i>

665
01:02:15,640 --> 01:02:16,760
"LORD PHOP"

666
01:02:19,600 --> 01:02:20,800
NO RESULTS FOUND

667
01:02:20,880 --> 01:02:22,760
NO RESULTS FOUND FOR "LORD PREECHAPIBAN"

668
01:02:22,840 --> 01:02:24,640
NO RESULTS FOR
"HIGH LORD PICHAYABHAKDI"

669
01:02:25,400 --> 01:02:27,000
<i>There is no information at all.</i>

670
01:02:27,920 --> 01:02:30,400
<i>Phop doesn't even exist</i>
<i>in the history books.</i>

671
01:02:32,000 --> 01:02:33,920
<i>Or do I wait for a meteor shower?</i>

672
01:02:34,880 --> 01:02:36,840
<i>Or do I have to wait until my birthday?</i>

673
01:02:43,600 --> 01:02:44,560
<i>Phop.</i>

674
01:02:46,320 --> 01:02:48,120
<i>I shall find my way back to you.</i>

675
01:04:40,120 --> 01:04:42,040
CHANCE OF SEEING
SHOOTING STARS IN AYUTTHAYA

676
01:04:45,120 --> 01:04:47,080
SHOOTING STARS CAN APPEAR
ANY MONTH, ALL YEAR

677
01:04:47,160 --> 01:04:48,680
THEY CAN BE SEEN 1-3 TIMES A MONTH

678
01:04:48,760 --> 01:04:50,280
DEPENDING ON HOW CLEAR THE SKY IS

679
01:04:53,800 --> 01:04:56,200
Your mom said
you're feeling a bit dazed, right?

680
01:04:56,280 --> 01:04:58,160
I brought you some vitamins.

681
01:05:05,360 --> 01:05:06,240
Jom!

682
01:05:13,360 --> 01:05:14,200
Jom…

683
01:05:16,520 --> 01:05:17,880
Who the hell is Jom?

684
01:05:18,680 --> 01:05:20,680
You miss me that much?

685
01:05:21,320 --> 01:05:22,160
I'm touched.

686
01:05:27,000 --> 01:05:27,840
You…

687
01:05:28,320 --> 01:05:29,480
You don't remember?

688
01:05:30,600 --> 01:05:31,440
Remember what?

689
01:05:31,520 --> 01:05:34,120
You're the one who doesn't remember me.

690
01:05:34,760 --> 01:05:35,760
You…

691
01:05:36,440 --> 01:05:37,560
Do you have amnesia?

692
01:05:51,800 --> 01:05:54,240
<i>Jom was probably Thee in a past life.</i>

693
01:05:55,840 --> 01:05:57,720
<i>Thee didn't travel through time</i>
<i>like I did.</i>

694
01:06:00,320 --> 01:06:01,960
Your mom is really worried.

695
01:06:02,640 --> 01:06:04,040
You refuse to leave your room,

696
01:06:04,120 --> 01:06:07,000
and at night,
you stay on the balcony until dawn.

697
01:06:07,080 --> 01:06:09,240
If you can't tell her, tell me instead.

698
01:06:12,280 --> 01:06:13,280
What's wrong?

699
01:06:19,200 --> 01:06:21,120
It's fine if you don't want to tell me.

700
01:06:22,280 --> 01:06:24,360
But you've missed a week of school.

701
01:06:25,760 --> 01:06:26,880
Wanna go back to the uni?

702
01:06:27,560 --> 01:06:30,080
Be with Pun and me.

703
01:06:31,280 --> 01:06:33,520
Maybe we can help you feel better.

704
01:06:37,400 --> 01:06:39,240
Pun is worried too, you know?

705
01:06:39,320 --> 01:06:41,280
He's sad too.

706
01:06:42,000 --> 01:06:43,280
That's why I'm sad too.

707
01:06:44,200 --> 01:06:45,080
Just look.

708
01:06:45,680 --> 01:06:46,680
I'm trying to smile,

709
01:06:47,760 --> 01:06:49,160
but I can't.

710
01:06:52,520 --> 01:06:53,360
See?

711
01:06:55,720 --> 01:06:57,040
Come back to the uni, please.

712
01:07:09,120 --> 01:07:10,320
Nakun.

713
01:07:11,720 --> 01:07:12,560
Nakun!

714
01:07:15,920 --> 01:07:17,360
Eat up, will you?

715
01:07:18,720 --> 01:07:20,280
We have classes all afternoon.

716
01:07:21,320 --> 01:07:22,160
Sorry.

717
01:07:22,640 --> 01:07:24,680
I was lost in my thoughts.

718
01:07:26,760 --> 01:07:27,600
But…

719
01:07:27,680 --> 01:07:29,480
you look so sad.

720
01:07:33,480 --> 01:07:34,680
Yeah, he's right.

721
01:07:35,200 --> 01:07:36,840
You can talk to us.

722
01:07:36,920 --> 01:07:37,920
It's okay.

723
01:07:41,680 --> 01:07:42,760
Thee.

724
01:07:43,400 --> 01:07:44,400
This isn't the time.

725
01:07:46,840 --> 01:07:47,880
Nakun,

726
01:07:48,600 --> 01:07:49,600
are you all right?

727
01:07:50,880 --> 01:07:52,800
Do you want to take the afternoon off?

728
01:07:57,800 --> 01:07:58,640
Thee.

729
01:07:59,200 --> 01:08:01,320
Should we take him back to his place?

730
01:08:06,000 --> 01:08:07,080
It's fine.

731
01:08:07,160 --> 01:08:08,360
Seriously?

732
01:08:09,160 --> 01:08:11,320
You've been zoning out all day.

733
01:08:12,160 --> 01:08:14,960
Have your misfortunes been upsetting you?

734
01:08:15,520 --> 01:08:19,000
Did you do what the fortune teller said
when you returned home?

735
01:08:21,200 --> 01:08:22,240
Guys…

736
01:08:24,240 --> 01:08:26,680
Can you take me to see the fortune teller?

737
01:08:28,960 --> 01:08:29,840
The fortune teller…

738
01:08:35,040 --> 01:08:37,720
Fortune teller, do you remember me?

739
01:08:40,160 --> 01:08:41,160
Indeed, I do.

740
01:08:42,800 --> 01:08:44,160
You were here the other day.

741
01:08:46,040 --> 01:08:46,920
No.

742
01:08:50,080 --> 01:08:51,319
What's on the menu tomorrow?

743
01:08:51,399 --> 01:08:54,240
-Anything works for me.
-Yeah.

744
01:08:58,040 --> 01:09:00,279
It's… It's Klao.

745
01:09:00,359 --> 01:09:01,240
Remember?

746
01:09:03,080 --> 01:09:04,399
My hair looks like a cow's?

747
01:09:07,760 --> 01:09:09,240
It looks fine to me.

748
01:09:10,399 --> 01:09:11,399
It's flowing.

749
01:09:11,479 --> 01:09:13,080
Fortune teller, I'm serious.

750
01:09:17,000 --> 01:09:17,840
I'm Klao,

751
01:09:18,399 --> 01:09:20,640
I live in Phop's house,

752
01:09:21,479 --> 01:09:22,720
and his mother is Lady Prayong.

753
01:09:23,279 --> 01:09:26,279
She's the lady who often gives you money.

754
01:09:29,160 --> 01:09:30,279
I do remember.

755
01:09:31,040 --> 01:09:32,000
Klao.

756
01:09:33,040 --> 01:09:34,000
I remember.

757
01:09:34,080 --> 01:09:35,439
You remember, don't you?

758
01:09:36,560 --> 01:09:39,680
If you do, could you tell me
how Phop is doing?

759
01:09:41,960 --> 01:09:45,319
Now that I've returned here,
is he still safe?

760
01:09:46,399 --> 01:09:47,359
I beg you.

761
01:09:47,439 --> 01:09:48,720
Please tell me.

762
01:09:48,800 --> 01:09:50,240
I can't take it anymore.

763
01:09:52,040 --> 01:09:53,000
If you want to know,

764
01:09:54,320 --> 01:09:55,480
I need to read your cards.

765
01:09:59,520 --> 01:10:00,360
Read my cards…

766
01:10:00,920 --> 01:10:01,960
For what?

767
01:10:02,720 --> 01:10:05,400
If you remember our past life,

768
01:10:05,480 --> 01:10:07,600
you must know about Phop.

769
01:10:30,520 --> 01:10:32,080
"Loss."

770
01:10:32,720 --> 01:10:33,960
"Separation."

771
01:10:35,880 --> 01:10:37,280
"A deep fear of change."

772
01:10:39,000 --> 01:10:39,840
Phop…

773
01:10:40,800 --> 01:10:42,560
The person you're thinking of…

774
01:10:45,400 --> 01:10:46,560
has met his fate.

775
01:11:00,840 --> 01:11:02,240
That's not true!

776
01:11:02,320 --> 01:11:04,000
-Nakun.
-Nakun, Nakun.

777
01:11:04,080 --> 01:11:05,040
Nakun.

778
01:11:05,520 --> 01:11:06,400
Nakun…

779
01:11:06,480 --> 01:11:07,800
Let me go!

780
01:11:14,400 --> 01:11:15,360
The stone.

781
01:11:15,440 --> 01:11:16,400
That stone.

782
01:11:17,840 --> 01:11:20,560
So you also traveled
back in time like I did?

783
01:11:23,080 --> 01:11:24,400
Nakun, enough.

784
01:11:25,000 --> 01:11:26,000
Did you?

785
01:11:27,360 --> 01:11:28,360
Let go!

786
01:11:28,440 --> 01:11:29,480
I told you to let go.

787
01:11:29,560 --> 01:11:31,160
Let go of me.

788
01:11:31,240 --> 01:11:32,400
Let go of me!

789
01:11:33,120 --> 01:11:34,840
Please, let go of me.

790
01:11:46,200 --> 01:11:47,360
Fortune teller.

791
01:11:50,760 --> 01:11:51,760
I beg you.

792
01:11:53,280 --> 01:11:54,400
Please…

793
01:11:54,480 --> 01:11:55,320
Can you…

794
01:11:55,840 --> 01:11:57,320
try to remember

795
01:11:58,280 --> 01:11:59,920
what happened to Phop?

796
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:01,320
Is he still safe?

797
01:12:03,000 --> 01:12:04,720
If you really don't know,

798
01:12:06,520 --> 01:12:10,240
can you tell me how I could travel
back in time to Ayutthaya?

799
01:12:11,240 --> 01:12:12,120
In your past life,

800
01:12:12,880 --> 01:12:15,200
you helped me so much.

801
01:12:16,760 --> 01:12:18,880
You were extraordinary!

802
01:12:20,280 --> 01:12:22,760
Why must you act so clueless in this life?

803
01:12:38,240 --> 01:12:39,120
Yes.

804
01:12:41,200 --> 01:12:43,360
I was better in my past life.

805
01:12:43,960 --> 01:12:46,400
<i>To let go of the old</i>
<i>is to welcome the new.</i>

806
01:12:49,600 --> 01:12:52,000
<i>A great change is upon us.</i>

807
01:12:52,800 --> 01:12:54,360
<i>An ending and a new beginning.</i>

808
01:12:54,920 --> 01:12:57,120
Lord Phop has met his end,

809
01:12:57,200 --> 01:12:58,920
yet he shall return once more.

810
01:13:08,600 --> 01:13:10,880
<i>Even the fortune teller is no help.</i>

811
01:13:12,400 --> 01:13:14,480
<i>I guess I have to let it go.</i>

812
01:13:20,320 --> 01:13:23,280
Our amuse-bouche comes
in the form of traditional Thai dishes

813
01:13:23,360 --> 01:13:24,640
with a modern twist.

814
01:13:28,160 --> 01:13:29,280
Sai!

815
01:13:29,360 --> 01:13:30,360
Yes?

816
01:13:31,760 --> 01:13:33,480
I'm really sorry, sir.

817
01:13:33,560 --> 01:13:36,080
We're sorry for the delay
in serving your food.

818
01:13:37,960 --> 01:13:39,320
That's not what I meant.

819
01:13:40,600 --> 01:13:43,400
I'm so sorry.
I thought you were someone else.

820
01:13:44,800 --> 01:13:45,720
Right.

821
01:13:53,480 --> 01:13:54,760
Thee.

822
01:13:54,840 --> 01:13:55,920
See?

823
01:13:56,000 --> 01:13:58,680
I told you to just get him a room here.

824
01:13:58,760 --> 01:14:00,360
Yet, you brought him to the rooftop.

825
01:14:00,440 --> 01:14:02,000
I'm sorry.

826
01:14:02,720 --> 01:14:03,680
I thought…

827
01:14:03,760 --> 01:14:07,520
if he could enjoy good food
with a scenic view,

828
01:14:08,200 --> 01:14:09,720
he might feel better.

829
01:14:15,440 --> 01:14:17,440
Hey, Pun.

830
01:14:18,440 --> 01:14:20,120
When did you get close to Thee?

831
01:14:23,560 --> 01:14:24,720
Well…

832
01:14:24,800 --> 01:14:28,440
since you were absent.

833
01:14:28,520 --> 01:14:31,280
After opening up to each other,

834
01:14:31,360 --> 01:14:34,680
I realized that he does have a soft side,

835
01:14:34,760 --> 01:14:36,760
beyond his constant joking.

836
01:14:43,200 --> 01:14:46,840
<i>My actions from my past life</i>
<i>really do affect the present day.</i>

837
01:14:50,760 --> 01:14:53,560
<i>So, would revealing</i>
<i>the truth about Klao's father</i>

838
01:14:54,240 --> 01:14:55,960
<i>have the same effect?</i>

839
01:14:59,720 --> 01:15:01,080
<i>If Sai…</i>

840
01:15:01,640 --> 01:15:02,840
<i>Jom…</i>

841
01:15:02,920 --> 01:15:04,080
<i>Kaew…</i>

842
01:15:04,160 --> 01:15:05,080
<i>The oracle…</i>

843
01:15:06,040 --> 01:15:08,000
<i>If they can reincarnate into this life,</i>

844
01:15:08,640 --> 01:15:11,080
<i>others might be able to as well.</i>

845
01:15:12,200 --> 01:15:13,200
<i>What about Phop?</i>

846
01:15:14,280 --> 01:15:16,240
<i>Did he reincarnate?</i>

847
01:15:17,080 --> 01:15:18,920
<i>Will he be able to remember me?</i>

848
01:15:23,120 --> 01:15:23,960
Nakun.

849
01:15:24,600 --> 01:15:25,520
Are you okay?

850
01:15:28,960 --> 01:15:29,800
I'm not.

851
01:15:32,440 --> 01:15:33,600
I'm sorry, Thee.

852
01:15:35,280 --> 01:15:37,600
Pun, please finish the food for me.

853
01:15:42,040 --> 01:15:42,920
Nakun.

854
01:15:48,720 --> 01:15:50,160
Don't force him.

855
01:15:50,240 --> 01:15:52,480
-But…
-But what?

856
01:15:53,040 --> 01:15:55,120
His feelings come first.

857
01:16:48,160 --> 01:16:51,800
THEE: ALMOST HERE, OR ANOTHER DAY?

858
01:16:51,880 --> 01:16:55,840
I'M HERE

859
01:17:12,760 --> 01:17:14,800
<i>I shall seek you out…</i>

860
01:17:14,880 --> 01:17:16,320
<i>until I find you</i>

861
01:17:16,400 --> 01:17:18,160
<i>and love you once more.</i>

862
01:17:34,720 --> 01:17:37,200
<i>In just a few weeks,</i>
<i>my life has changed a lot.</i>

863
01:17:37,280 --> 01:17:38,160
Let me help.

864
01:17:38,240 --> 01:17:40,440
<i>And in this new life</i>
<i>I'm trying to get used to,</i>

865
01:17:41,000 --> 01:17:42,880
<i>I've met familiar faces from my past life.</i>

866
01:17:42,960 --> 01:17:44,560
A-Chai? Who?

867
01:17:45,800 --> 01:17:47,880
<i>You! Are you all right?</i>

868
01:17:47,960 --> 01:17:49,320
When you called me,

869
01:17:49,400 --> 01:17:50,680
I thought you knew me.

870
01:17:50,760 --> 01:17:53,080
No. I was calling "you" as a pronoun.

871
01:17:54,280 --> 01:17:57,600
Since Nakun left for Ayutthaya,
I've only been dreaming of these things.

872
01:17:57,680 --> 01:18:00,240
It feels like I once fell for you, Thee.

873
01:18:00,320 --> 01:18:01,440
But you…

874
01:18:02,160 --> 01:18:03,920
You kept rejecting me.

875
01:18:04,000 --> 01:18:05,680
CAN YOU HELP ME GET BACK TO AYUTTHAYA?

876
01:18:06,520 --> 01:18:07,880
Let's take in the scenery.

877
01:18:07,960 --> 01:18:09,920
It's as pristine as it was back then.

878
01:18:10,920 --> 01:18:11,920
You…

879
01:18:12,000 --> 01:18:14,000
Your memories
have always been there, right?
